    16	- 7 calendar days TEST;
    17	- 1 calendar day embargo;
    18	- repeat with a 16-day cycle.
    19	
    20	That rule and its defaults are executable at `src/mcrl/env/ephemeris.py:182-266`; available dates are filtered from actual archive filenames at `src/mcrl/env/ephemeris.py:268-283`; its serialized identity is at `src/mcrl/env/ephemeris.py:301-310`. The frozen preregistration independently records `block_days=7`, `embargo_days=1`, `first_block_part=train`, 166 TRAIN files, 160 TEST files, 47 embargo files, and a minimum TRAIN/TEST gap of two days (`artifacts/PREREG-FROZEN-2026-08-25-R2.json:2794-2805`).
    21	
    22	The normal V0.25 provider is fail-closed against TEST content: it precomputes the TEST-date set and refuses `load()` for those dates (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:145-158`); a forced non-TRAIN start is rejected before a TLE load (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:161-195`); and the normal seed-derived start is drawn only from the TRAIN date list and checked again (`src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:201-211`). Thus a world built through this provider cannot have a TEST start date or read a TEST file. Because of the one-day embargo, its date-1/date/date+1 element window also cannot reach a TEST day from a TRAIN start.
