+
+**What is established and what this decision changes**
+
+**Verified.** The contract evaluates on TRAIN and explicitly says “no TEST.” Its coordination claim requires held-out realised pooled EE. The primary learned experiment compares informative versus neutral source training, retaining all heads, and its three FULL-versus-DROP contrasts form an intersection–union conjunction. The endpoint is pooled ΣB/ΣE; the lower 2.5th percentile must exceed +0.5% relative. These are different questions from whether a bounded oracle beats unilateral search. [H/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:19–31.]
+
+**Verified.** The September 9 open-decision record names additional-date world generation as the longest-lead blocked item. It records options, not an allocation. Its suggestion that training dates are abundant is contradicted by the subsequent archive erratum. [C/V025-CONTROLLER-OPEN-DECISION-EVAL-DATE-POOL-2026-09-09.md:23–36; C/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ARCHIVE-AND-GROWTH-2026-09-09.md:41–48.]
+
+**Verified, executable finding.** The guard is real, but incomplete: it rejects a CLAIM_PANEL date accompanied by **any other supplied role**, including a training role if supplied. However, mandatory development roles are only PROBE, CALIBRATION, REHEARSAL, KAT, SYNTHETIC_REAL and SMOKE. Manifest construction requires those roles and CLAIM_PANEL, but neither requires training-source identities nor reconciles against the source corpus. Thus “never compares” in DATE-VARIANCE:22 means **no compulsory comparison against actual training provenance**, not that the predicate is incapable of comparing a training row. The emitted freshness flag is not proof of source exclusion. [W/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:195–204,5726–5777.]
+
+**Verified, written rule.** The freshness amendment says “any successor development activity,” then enumerates roles without training; another declaration literally says “source generation and training on the claim panel.” Source disjointness was therefore neither completely enforced nor unambiguously specified. This decision makes it compulsory for the learned claim. The existing uppercase TEST exclusion remains unchanged; this creates no TEST split. [C/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.5-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:7–9; C/V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md:12–16; W/src/mcrl/physics_v025/provider_legacy.py:145–158.]
+
+**Must dates be disjoint? The estimation answer**
+
+**Derived.** Date overlap is not intrinsically biased. Fix the historical archive A, training information T, fitted policies π(T), date weights w_d and within-date scenario distribution Z. If evaluation scenarios are independent of training conditional on A and their dates, and policies and analysis are frozen, then for an additive paired outcome g,
+
+`E[Σ_d w_d mean_i g(π(T), A_d, Z_di) | A,T] = Σ_d w_d E_Z[g(π(T), A_d,Z)].`
+
+This estimates fresh-scenario performance on that fixed familiar-date distribution even when training used the same dates. It does not estimate performance on unseen dates. For pooled EE the unbiased pieces are bits and energy totals; their finite-sample ratio is not generally unbiased. A second-order ratio bias is approximately `μ_B Var(E_hat)/μ_E^3 − Cov(B_hat,E_hat)/μ_E^2`. Date disjointness does not itself remove that ratio bias.
+
+**Derived.** For an unseen-date contrast, overlap can instead introduce *differential training-exposure benefit*. In a simple equally weighted additive model, let f be the evaluation mass on exposed dates and b_F,b_D be FULL's and DROP's mean exposure benefits relative to the corresponding unexposed performance. Then the overlap contribution to contrast bias is `f(b_F−b_D)`. Pairing cancels common shocks, not unequal exposure benefits. FULL-minus-S_UNI can be especially asymmetric when only FULL is fitted. The sign can be positive or negative. For pooled ratios the corresponding calculation must use arm-specific bits/energy contributions and their weights, not simply the fraction of calendar dates.
+
+**Verified → Derived.** The receipts supply no controlled trained-versus-untrained exposure contrast. The one-date learner finding cannot estimate a between-date effect; CEILING30-MARGIN explicitly contains no learner or training run. Consequently the receipts provide **no nontrivial numerical bound on overlap bias**, and 0.751% is not such a bound. The observed minimum/maximum of oracle gains do not bound learned counterfactuals. A useful finite relative-effect bound would additionally require bounds on performance and a positive comparator-EE floor not supplied by these receipts; the contract even permits zero bits and records undefined comparator-zero draws. [C/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDING-ONE-DATE-2026-09-09.md:11–18; M/CEILING30-MARGIN-2026-09-10.md:3–5,29–35; H/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:30.]
+
+**UNDETERMINED — numerical overlap bias.** The single settling experiment is a temporally stratified, randomised source-date-inclusion experiment: matched training budgets and learner seeds, policies trained with versus without the assigned dates, evaluated on the same fresh within-date worlds, reporting the difference-in-differences for each claimed contrast. A retrospective comparison of easy exposed dates against different unexposed dates would not identify this effect. This experiment is not a prerequisite for the allocation and is not run here.
+
+**Decision.** Require disjoint **world start dates** for claim evaluation versus all informative and neutral training sources, fitted preprocessing, warm starts, calibration, and development outcomes. This protects the interpretation “evaluation on source-excluded TRAIN start dates within the frozen historical archive” without needing an unsupported bound on training exposure. Overlap remains acceptable for learner-free development diagnostics and for an explicitly conditional familiar-date benchmark; those results cannot substitute for this learned confirmation panel.
+
+**Decision, scope of separation.** No additional calendar buffer is imposed. The provider uses date−1/date/date+1 files, so neighbouring source and evaluation starts can share exogenous TLE inputs. Disjoint file windows would require at least three calendar days between starts, and still would not establish independent constellations. We permit that shared exogenous archive and prohibit shared generated worlds, trajectories, labelled anchors and fitted evaluation information. This is a start-date holdout, not a claim of unseen orbital records, future-constellation generalisation or independent daily geometry. That narrower interpretation is deliberate; a costly new embargo has no receipt-supported bias reduction here. [Verified window: W/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/probe/run_v025_matrix_probe.py:5778–5783; W/src/mcrl/env/ephemeris.py:97–113. Derived separation distance: two ±1-day windows are disjoint when their centres differ by at least three days.]
