+**Decision, why 48.** It is a fixed, temporally spread resource allocation, not a fitted optimum: eight dates in each of six calendar strata while leaving substantial source diversity. A 48-date resource envelope and the same six-stratum construction were already proposed before the corrected 30-date result existed. This decision now makes the allocation concrete and uses the supplied SD to assess its limits, rather than choosing dates or a target effect from observed gains. [Historical proposal only: A/DATEPOOL-ADJUDICATION-2026-09-09.md:49,70,74–88.]
