+**Decision.** No new archive dates are required to implement the adopted allocation. More worlds on its dates are required. World generation can now be scheduled against S and E without another allocation decision; all independent physics/admission and integrity gates continue to apply. This adjudication launches nothing. The ladder allowance includes search/evaluation and is not a measured cost for full source labelling, 16-seed training, or two-world-per-date full-horizon claim evaluation. Their total wall time is **UNDETERMINED**; one representative end-to-end contracted date receipt at a fixed four-process cap would settle the per-date cost. Generating worlds cannot manufacture the 112 missing calendar dates in the rejected 160-date layout: that would first require a separately frozen archive expansion, never TEST reuse.
+
+**Strongest case against this allocation, and answer**
+
+The strongest objection is that 48 is an engineering envelope supported by variance from the wrong experiment. It reduces a sealed 160-date panel; the measured oracle SD need not match learned FULL-versus-DROP pooled influence variance; neighbouring dates can remain dependent; and holding out dates does not guarantee useful learning from the source pool. Even the date-only +0.75% sensitivity needs 71 dates. A conditional familiar-date evaluation with independently generated worlds could validly overlap source dates and preserve more evaluation coverage. The two historically conflicting reservations and incomplete global lineage further weaken any blanket claim of freshness. These objections follow from the estimand distinction, arithmetic and enforcement findings above, not from whether a preferred route won.
+
+**Answer and final ruling.** I accept those limitations and reject the claim that a 160-date calibration already certifies this experiment. I nevertheless choose **116 source/development, 48 evaluation-only, two quarantined**, because it fixes the missing operational boundary, preserves broad training support and clean start-date evaluation, and is compatible with measured date-only precision at the pre-existing +2% planning alternative without consuming TEST or choosing favourable outcomes. The panel estimates performance on these source-excluded historical TRAIN starts; it is not asserted to be a probability sample of all 166 dates. Actual claim power and residual date dependence must be reported honestly, and failure remains an admissible outcome. The allocation is final; uncertainty about efficacy is not authority to change its dates, margins, model or sign rules after results.
+
